# reserve-grant-independence — nothing an actor can be granted lets it past a human
# referral. `bot` is granted at both gates and its granted L3 meets each gate's required
# L3, so step (4) would dispose `auto`. At g1 the token's kind `audit` matches the
# reservation, and step (3) fires regardless: `reserved` is evaluated on the kind,
# independent of which actor presents it (specification §7.1). g2 is the control — the
# same maximally-privileged actor, the same grade, an unreserved kind: `auto`.
#
# This is corrigibility as the language states it. The human referral is not an
# exception a grant can outrank; it is not evaluated against the grant at all.
actor bot grade L3
human ombud role ombud
gate  g1  risk low  grade L3  grant bot
gate  g2  risk low  grade L3  grant bot
reserve audit by ombud
cord  bot -> g1
cord  bot -> g2
cord  g1  -> master
cord  g2  -> master
